    <!-- How to play -->
    <string name="tp_howto_name">Teen Patti</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_tagline">Three cards each — the best hand takes the pot.</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_pill">3 to 6 players · table chips only</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_goal_title">Goal</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_goal_1">Win pots by holding the best three cards — or by being the last player who hasn\'t packed.</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_goal_2">The table goes on hand after hand until you leave. Everyone starts with the same chips, anyone who runs out gets a fresh stack, and chips never leave the table.</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_deal_title">Each hand</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_deal_1">Everyone puts the boot into the pot and gets three cards face down.</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_deal_2">Play goes round from the dealer\'s left.</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_deal_3">You can play BLIND (without looking) or tap SEE to look at your cards at any time. Once seen, you stay seen.</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_bet_title">Your turn</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_bet_1">CHAAL: a blind player pays the current stake; a seen player pays twice the stake.</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_bet_2">RAISE: pay double that, and the stake doubles for everyone (up to a limit).</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_bet_3">PACK: give up the hand. Chips you already put in stay in the pot.</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_bet_4">Playing blind is cheaper, but you don\'t know what you hold.</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_bet_5">If you can\'t afford a chaal, you can go ALL IN: every hand still in is shown at once.</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_show_title">Show and sideshow</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_show_1">SHOW: when only two players are left, pay a chaal to compare both hands. The better hand takes the pot; on a tie, the player who asked loses.</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_show_2">SIDESHOW: when you are seen and three or more players are left, pay a chaal to ask the seen player before you to compare privately. If they accept, the lower hand packs (on a tie, you pack). They may decline.</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_show_3">When everyone else packs, the last player takes the pot without showing.</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_rank_title">Hand rankings</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_rank_1">Best first: Trail (three of a kind) · Pure sequence · Sequence · Colour · Pair · High card.</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_rank_2">A-K-Q is the top sequence. By default A-2-3 is second; you can make it the lowest in setup.</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_rank_3">Inside a kind, compare the highest card, then the next. Suits never break a tie.</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_tips_title">Tips</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_tips_1">A pair or better is a strong hand: almost three hands in four are only a high card.</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_tips_2">Watch who keeps paying after seeing their cards — they are often holding something.</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_tips_3">Packing early is cheap. Don\'t chase a weak hand when the stake gets high.</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_ex_1">A trail of Queens: only a higher trail beats it.</string>
    <string name="tp_howto_ex_2">A-2-3 in mixed suits: a sequence, second only to A-K-Q by default.</string>

